# Scope and stopping
- Done means the stated scope is satisfied and the repo's existing checks pass. That is the completion signal; do not invent an additional one.
- The stated scope is the whole deliverable. Finish it, then stop and report. Adjacent problems you notice get reported, not fixed.
- Verification is whatever the repo already provides — its tests, its build, its version control. If a change would need a check the repo does not have, say so rather than building one.
- If two readings of a request lead to materially different work, stop and ask for clarification.
